  "sourceSummary": "CriticalBody original Incline Cable Curl by Liam Brown: compact cable machine variant mimics incline dumbbell curl with arms near sides and may be seated; original separately describes wide cable crossover30degree version and explicitly allows45degree bench. This implements compact dual low pulleys with45degree back support and bilateral supinated D-handles. It is not the wide30degree crossover protocol.",
  "motion": "Bilateral seated45degree incline cable curl. Fixed upperarms slightly behind torso line with modest lateral abduction. Supinated D-handles curl in parallel forward/up planes, back supported and feet planted. Two procedural towers each have extended low pulley and floor return idler to preserve arm clearance. Smooth phases0.4/3.8/4.2/7.6.",
